    <p>Speed is the only weak point. At Q8 a dense 12B is memory-bandwidth-bound here, so generation stays around 14 to 15 tokens per second across all three backends. ROCm leads prompt processing at 928 against RADV's 716, but generation barely moves. A Q4 build would roughly double throughput at some quality cost, so Q8 stays the quality reference until a lower-precision run proves itself.</p>
